From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: server, win32u: another process's child window keeps what it draws

David's dev box (2026-11-15): DevToys 2 -- WPF with Mica hosting a WebView2
control -- had a black client area (the desktop through it under the
desktop compositor). Chromium's GPU process draws the page into a window of
its own inside WPF's, with GDI (our DirectComposition), and only when the
page changes. Two things lost what it drew:

- Its DC kept WPF's old X window after WPF made a new one with alpha for
  its Mica: win32u brings a DC's visible region up to date every time only
  for another process's window, not for a window of ours in another
  process's top-level, which that process moves, clips and gives a new X
  window without telling us. Every frame then failed (RENDER BadPicture).
  Such a DC is now brought up to date every time.
- WPF's drawing over its whole client (the WebView2 host is
  WS_EX_TRANSPARENT, which its parent's drawing is not clipped by) was
  flushed from its window surface over the page. A child window of another
  process than the surface's draws straight into the X window and is never
  drawn by the surface's process, so it is now left out of the surface,
  frame and all, as a swap chain's area is; a transparent child is passed
  over only when nothing of another process or with a pixel format is in
  it. The child's process tells the surface's process when the child moves,
  appears or goes (WM_WINE_CLIENT_SURFACE with delta 0), after it has let
  go of the window (a message sent under the user lock aborts).

On Windows the compositor keeps such content above its parents' drawing.

Gate: test/xprocdc-gate.sh (make test-xprocdc): a host with a transparent
child, a render process's red child in it drawn once: red after the host
fills its whole client, red drawn again after the host turns glass (a new
32-bit X window), red after another fill. Mutants
SG_MUTANT_FOREIGN_CHILD_IN_SURFACE, SG_MUTANT_FOREIGN_CHILD_NO_NOTIFY and
SG_MUTANT_XPROC_TOP_STALE_DC each fail it.
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/dce.c b/dlls/win32u/dce.c
index 764306e..7b8eed4 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/dce.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/dce.c
@@ -1558,6 +1558,15 @@ HDC WINAPI NtUserGetDCEx( HWND hwnd, HRGN clip_rgn, DWORD flags )
 
     /* cross-process invalidation is not supported yet, so always update the vis rgn */
     if (!is_current_process_window( hwnd )) update_vis_rgn = TRUE;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_XPROC_TOP_STALE_DC
+    /* Stained Glass OS: ...nor for a window of ours in another process's
+     * top-level, which that process moves, sizes, clips and gives a new X
+     * window (a visual with alpha for Mica or glass) without telling us:
+     * Chromium's GPU process kept drawing a WebView2 control (its
+     * DirectComposition target, under DevToys' WPF window) into the X window
+     * WPF had replaced -- BadPicture for every frame, the page black */
+    else if (!is_current_process_window( NtUserGetAncestor( hwnd, GA_ROOT ) )) update_vis_rgn = TRUE;
+#endif
 
     if (set_dce_flags( dce->hdc, DCHF_VALIDATEVISRGN )) update_vis_rgn = TRUE;  /* DC was dirty */
 
